---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

// Privacy policy for this website and the browser-based tools it hosts.
// The public pages run Google Analytics 4 (Layout.astro, gated on
// PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID) and load the catalog from Firestore, so
// this page has to say so. The Google Play apps have
// their own stand-alone policy at /privacy/apps (the Play listing URL).
const effective = "September 17, 2026";
// Contact for privacy questions. Change here only.
const contact = "sheibeck@gmail.com";
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Darktier Studios website privacy policy — what the site and its browser-based tools collect, what stays in your browser, and how to opt out of analytics."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section style="padding:84px 0 28px">
      <p class="kicker">Darktier Studios · legal</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 0 -0.06em">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-meta">Effective {effective} · {site.legalName}, {site.location}</p>
    </section>

    <article class="privacy">
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        The short version: this website uses <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to count visits, and
        nothing else about you. Our browser-based tools keep their data in your own browser. We never sell
        or share personal data. Our Google Play apps run on your device and have
        <a href="/privacy/apps">their own policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who this covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to <a href={site.url}>{site.url}</a> and the browser-based companion tools
        hosted on it (The Armory). It does not cover our mobile apps on Google Play — see the
        <a href="/privacy/apps">privacy policy for our apps</a> — or external tools we link to, which are
        separate services with their own privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        The public pages of this site use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to measure traffic: which
        pages are visited, roughly where visitors come from, what kind of device and browser they use, and
        how long they stay. Google Analytics sets cookies and assigns a random identifier to tell one
        visitor from another; it does not tell us who you are, and we do not link analytics data to names
        or email addresses. Google processes this data on our behalf under
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        We use it to see which games and tools people care about. We do not use it for advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        To opt out, install
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's browser add-on</a>,
        block third-party scripts, or clear cookies for this site.
      </p>

      <h3>Hosting and the games catalog</h3>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on Google's Firebase platform, and the catalog of games, tools, and news is
        loaded from Google's Firestore database. Like any web host, Google may record standard server logs
        (such as your IP address and browser type) to deliver the pages. We do not access those logs to
        identify you.
      </p>

      <h3>Browser-based tools (The Armory)</h3>
      <p>
        Companion apps that run on this site, such as Burning Banners and Fate of the Fellowship, save
        their game state in your browser's local storage so you can pick up where you left off. That data
        stays in your browser: it is never sent to us, and clearing your browser's site data removes it.
      </p>

      <h3>What we don't do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising networks, ad tracking, or sale of personal data</li>
        <li>No accounts, sign-ups, newsletters, or contact forms that store your details</li>
        <li>No collection of location, contacts, or payment information</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The only cookies this site sets are Google Analytics cookies (names beginning with <code>_ga</code>),
        used to distinguish visitors and sessions. Our browser-based tools use local storage, not cookies.
        You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings; the site works without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for a general audience and does not knowingly collect personal information
        from children under 13. Analytics data is aggregated and not tied to any individual.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Apart from aggregated analytics, we hold no personal data about you, so there is nothing for us to
        export, correct, or erase. You control the Analytics cookies and the local storage in your own
        browser. If you have a question about data you believe we hold, contact us and we will answer.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we update this policy, the new version will be posted at this address with a new effective date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a><br />
        {site.legalName} · {site.location}
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
